\DOC X86_QUICKSIM_TAC

\TYPE {X86_QUICKSIM_TAC : thm * (thm option array) -> term list -> int list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Discharges an {ensures}-style x86 machine-code correctness goal by symbolically
simulating a specified range of instruction steps, closing the goal outright.

\DESCRIBE
{execth : thm * (thm option array)} pairs the code-length theorem with the
precomputed per-instruction decoding table for the program under verification;
{pats : term list} lists state-component read patterns (with the state variable
left schematic) to be tracked during the simulation; {snums : int list} gives,
as a numeric range, the step numbers over which the simulation runs. The goal's
conclusion must be an {ensures x86} triple with a precondition, a postcondition
and a {MAYCHANGE} frame, with the bounds and non-overlap side conditions among
the assumptions {A}.
{
   A ?- t
   =================  X86_QUICKSIM_TAC execth pats snums
}
\noindent In all observed traces the postcondition's main conjunction is
guarded by a hypothesis contradicted by one of the assumptions in {A}, so the
simulation only has to establish the final program-counter value.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this one outcome, on goals of this single shape
with the full assumption context present.

\ENDDOC
